{"id":"d08","name":"Evaluate a Metric Formula","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["tokens"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A dashboard stores metric formulas in <b>reverse Polish notation</b>: each operator comes after its two operands, so <code>[\"3\", \"4\", \"+\", \"2\", \"*\"]</code> means <code>(3 + 4) * 2</code>. Tokens are integers (possibly negative) or one of <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>*</code>, <code>/</code>.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the value of the formula. Division is integer division that <b>truncates toward zero</b> (<code>-7 / 2</code> gives <code>-3</code>). The formula is always valid and never divides by zero.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>tokens = [\"3\", \"4\", \"+\", \"2\", \"*\"]</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">14</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.string tokens<br><b>[output]</b> integer</div>","starter":"def solution(tokens):\n    # write your code here\n    return 0\n","hints":["Un nombre : empile. Un opérateur : dépile b PUIS a, calcule a op b, empile.","Attention : -7 // 2 vaut -4 en Python. Tronquer vers zéro : int(a / b)."],"summary_fr":"Évaluer une formule en notation polonaise inverse (+ - * /) avec une pile ; la division est entière et tronque vers zéro.","tags":["DSA","pile","notation polonaise inverse","division entière vers zéro"],"minutes":12,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tokens":["3","4","+","2","*"]},"expected":{"value":14}},{"input":{"tokens":["-7","2","/"]},"expected":{"value":-3}}],"hidden_n":10,"hidden":"","solution":""}